            "type_1_dim3_label": "Adventure",
            "type_1_dim3_value": 38,
            "type_1_locked_text": "Your desire grows through response. A lingering look, a change in someone’s voice, or the feeling that their attention keeps returning to you can be more powerful than anything overt. What pulls you in is knowing that your presence is affecting someone — that you are not simply involved in the moment, but quietly becoming its center.\n\nYou’re especially responsive to focused attention, verbal appreciation, and a partner who takes time to notice what makes you react. Feeling admired helps you relax, but feeling genuinely wanted is what allows your desire to fully surface.\n\nYour hidden turn-on may be more active than it appears: beneath the wish to be pursued is a desire to influence the entire experience without having to ask for control directly.\n\nYour desire pattern: you’re most easily turned on when attention becomes unmistakable desire—and you can feel someone responding specifically to you.",
            "type_2_name": "The Dreamer",
            "type_2_tagline": "Reality rarely turns you on as much as what your mind can turn it into.",
            "type_2_percent": 14,
            "type_2_dim1_label": "Dominance",
            "type_2_dim1_value": 36,
            "type_2_dim2_label": "Intensity",
            "type_2_dim2_value": 55,
            "type_2_dim3_label": "Adventure",
            "type_2_dim3_value": 76,
            "type_2_locked_text": "Your desire often begins before anything actually happens. A voice, a fictional scenario, a sense of anticipation, or one carefully chosen detail can open an entire world in your mind. Once that inner world feels real enough, your body is much more willing to follow.\n\nYou’re not simply attracted to romance or atmosphere. You respond to context: who you are in the scene, what has led to this moment, and what might happen next. Story gives your desire permission to move beyond everyday reality and explore feelings you may not express as directly elsewhere.\n\nYour hidden turn-on is transformation. You may be drawn to experiences that let you temporarily become a different version of yourself—bolder, more surrendered, more mysterious, or completely free from your usual role.\n\nYour desire pattern: your imagination is not an accessory to pleasure; it is often the place where pleasure begins.",
            "type_3_name": "The Switch",
            "type_3_tagline": "Your real turn-on isn’t control or surrender. It’s the moment one becomes the other.",
            "type_3_percent": 21,
            "type_3_dim1_label": "Dominance",
            "type_3_dim1_value": 68,
            "type_3_dim2_label": "Intensity",
            "type_3_dim2_value": 88,
            "type_3_dim3_label": "Adventure",
            "type_3_dim3_value": 82,
            "type_3_locked_text": "Your desire resists fixed roles. Sometimes you want to set the pace, provoke a reaction, and feel someone respond to your confidence. At other times, what excites you most is meeting someone whose presence is strong enough that you willingly stop directing the moment.\n\nThe shift depends less on labels and more on chemistry. Trust, mood, confidence, and the other person’s energy can completely change what you want. Predictability may feel safe, but contrast is what keeps your attention alive.\n\nYour hidden turn-on is being surprised by yourself. The hottest moments are often the ones that reveal a reaction or appetite you did not expect to have.\n\nYour desire pattern: you’re most easily turned on by responsive power—the freedom to take control, give it away, and feel the dynamic change in real time.",
            "type_4_name": "The Director",
            "type_4_tagline": "You don’t want to wait for the right moment. You want to decide exactly how it unfolds.",
            "type_4_percent": 11,
            "type_4_dim1_label": "Adventure",
            "type_4_dim1_value": 94,
            "type_4_dim2_label": "Intensity",
            "type_4_dim2_value": 80,
            "type_4_dim3_label": "Adventure",
            "type_4_dim3_value": 56,
            "type_4_locked_text": "You don’t just want to participate in an experience—you want to shape it. You naturally notice pacing, reactions, and exactly when the energy should build, pause, or change. Expressing what you want does not pull you out of the moment; it makes the moment feel more real.\n\nYou’re especially responsive to someone who listens closely, follows confidently, and gives you visible feedback. Their reaction confirms that your choices are having an effect, and that sense of influence often intensifies your own pleasure.\n\nYour hidden turn-on is not simply control. It is responsiveness. You don’t want a passive audience; you want someone whose reactions give you new information and inspire your next move.\n\nYour desire pattern: you’re most easily turned on when you can guide the pace, shape the experience, and watch your intention become someone else’s reaction.",
